<title>UK: Perkins first half pretax profit edges up.</title>
<headline>Perkins first half pretax profit edges up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		4.1		    vs 3.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.75		   vs 1.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     11.1		   vs 10.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   241.8		  vs 228.5</p>
<p> Operating result	 12.3		   vs 11.8</p>
<p> Interest		   1.2		    vs 1.4</p>
<p> Tax			  4.1		    vs 3.6</p>
<p> Net taxed		  7.0		    vs 6.8</p>
<p> Retained profit	  2.8		    vs 2.6</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 15</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 15  Ex-div date		October 7</p>
<p>Note - Perkins Foods Plc said it expected further growth in the second half. &quot;Product initiatives and efficiency improvements will impact positively on the Frozen Foods division's results for the full year. The outlook for the Chilled Foods and Fresh Produce divisions remains good,&quot; chief executive Howard Phillips said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
